# BLOCKED -- capability gap, not wording drift. A script's module identity
# authority is rooted at the script's OWN directory
# (src/module/xmodule_identity.c:320), so importing `../../fixtures/...` is
# refused as "module '...' escapes or lacks its identity authority"
# (src/module/xmodule_resolver.c:318) before the frontend ever runs. The
# assertion below is what this case demands; it stays red until relative
# imports may leave the entry script's directory.
#
# The wording and position below were confirmed against the compiler by
# compiling the same program with the fixture copied beside it. No error code is
# pinned: any case with an `import` takes the module-graph path, which prints
# the uncoded `file:line:col: error: msg` form (src/app/cli/xcmd_run.c:484)
# rather than the frontend's `error[E0352]:` rendering.
